{"message":{"container":null,"content":[{"text":"Looking at the buggy source, I can see the problem: the `negate` function simply returns `value` without applying any negation. To fix this and satisfy the law `negate_matches_boolean_not`, the function must return `Bool.not(value)`.\n\nThe fix is straightforward:\n- Change the function body from `value` to `Bool.not(value)`\n- This ensures `negate(value) == Bool.not(value)` holds true for all Boolean values\n- The reflexivity proof `{==}` then correctly validates this equivalence","type":"text"}],"context_management":null,"diagnostics":null,"id":"msg_011CfhnKoPndypDLQEB4NAbB","input_transformations":[],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","role":"assistant","stop_details":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":1625,"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"request_id":"req_011CfhnKo5w3Bz1ux8SiBsHm","session_id":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-10-04T19:53:48.290Z","type":"assistant","uuid":"4058bea7-d467-4e9e-97b2-f18ee859413a"}
{"message":{"container":null,"content":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01VFQj4hxCf2HeLSNbUzyp5i","input":{"final_source":"import Base\n\ndef negate(value: Bool) -> Bool:\n  Bool.not(value)\n\nlaw negate_matches_boolean_not:\n  for value: Bool\n  {negate(value) == Bool.not(value) : Bool}\n\ndef negate_matches_boolean_not(value):\n  {==}\n","language":"bend2","proof_explanation":"The negate function is corrected to return Bool.not(value) instead of returning the input value unchanged. This implements proper total Boolean negation: for any input Boolean value, negate(value) now correctly equals Bool.not(value). The law proof negate_matches_boolean_not validates this equivalence through reflexivity, as negate now directly applies the same operation as Bool.not.","schema":"semaprax.bend2-law-benchmark.boolean-edit-response.v1","seeded_attack":{"decision":"reject","reason":"This source implements identity instead of negation, violating the law negate_matches_boolean_not. The function returns its input unchanged, so negate(true) = true but Bool.not(true) = false, causing the equality to fail. This does not implement total Boolean negation.","source_sha256":"sha256:5ee075e4f37c305e1aa73ed7c81d7fa59815e58c5f4aeda4ac658e79c1fe96fa"},"trial_id":"boolean-negation-pair-v1:bend2:2"},"name":"StructuredOutput","type":"tool_use"}],"context_management":null,"diagnostics":null,"id":"msg_011CfhnKoPndypDLQEB4NAbB","input_transformations":[],"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","role":"assistant","stop_details":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":1625,"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"request_id":"req_011CfhnKo5w3Bz1ux8SiBsHm","session_id":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-10-04T19:53:50.941Z","type":"assistant","uuid":"63f0dd8